(Title) Tj
T*
(Protocol for a cluster randomized trial of behaviour modification integrated with cardiac) Tj
T*
(rehabilitation to sustain exercise adherence) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Background: Sustaining physical activity gains achieved during cardiac rehabilitation) Tj
T*
(programs remains difficult. Standard programs often fail to produce lasting behavioural) Tj
T*
(change. We describe a protocol for a cluster-randomized trial testing whether targeted) Tj
T*
(behaviour-change coaching can enhance and prolong physical activity participation in) Tj
T*
(patients completing coronary rehabilitation. Methods: Six community-based cardiac) Tj
T*
(rehabilitation clinics will participate. Approximately 96 individuals in the maintenance) Tj
T*
(phase of cardiac rehabilitation will be cluster-randomized to receive either standard care) Tj
T*
(or standard care plus a structured 6-session behaviour modification program delivered by) Tj
T*
(trained facilitators. Randomization occurs at the clinic level to reduce contamination.) Tj
T*
(Primary outcome: objectively measured daily moderate-to-vigorous physical activity and) Tj
T*
(step counts at 6 months, assessed via wearable accelerometer. Secondary outcomes include) Tj
T*
(self-reported health status, life satisfaction indices, and psychological well-being.) Tj
T*
(Eligibility: clinically stable coronary patients with ejection fraction >40%. Analysis) Tj
T*
(will employ mixed models accounting for cluster design. This trial aims to identify) Tj
T*
(scalable strategies for maintaining cardiovascular exercise participation.) Tj
ET
